# Wain — static export on Apache / LiteSpeed (Hostinger)
#
# Next.js `output: 'export'` with `trailingSlash: true` writes each route as a
# directory containing index.html, so no rewrite-to-index catch-all is needed
# — and must NOT be added, as it would mask real 404s.

ErrorDocument 404 /404.html
DirectoryIndex index.html

# Never serve this file itself.
<Files ".htaccess">
  Require all denied
</Files>

# Directories without an index.html — /_next/static/chunks/ and friends —
# must not answer with a file listing. Usually off at the host, but "usually"
# is not a setting.
Options -Indexes

# Dotfiles are never content here.
<FilesMatch "^\.">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the previous site left behind
#
# wainkw.com's document root is not empty. Before this export existed it ran a
# single-file HTML app with a PHP back end, and that is still sitting there:
# api.php, admin.html, an admin token, ~28 index.bak-*.html copies, two zipped
# archives of the whole site, and wain.db — a live SQLite database.
#
# The .htaccess it shipped denied wain.db. This file replaces that one, so
# these rules have to come with it. Dropping a static-export .htaccess on top
# of that server without them would put a 94KB database on the public web.
#
# These deny access; they do not delete anything. Removing the files is a
# separate decision that belongs to whoever knows if the old app still runs.

<FilesMatch "^wain\.db">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# A 60-byte credential in the web root, next to the admin panel it belongs to.
# It should be rotated and moved out; until then it must not be downloadable.
<Files "admin.token">
  Require all denied
</Files>

# Backups and archives of the site, served under guessable names —
# index.bak-300.html, index.bak-301.html, and two zips of everything.
<FilesMatch "\.(bak|zip|db|sqlite|sqlite3)$|^index\.bak|\.broken-|\.bak-">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Scratch output from the old deploy scripts: 52 files, including ones named
# sec-out.txt and keys-out.txt.
<FilesMatch "-out\.txt$|^admin\.token$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The rest of what is actually in that docroot.
#
# The rules above were written from a directory listing. The docroot has since
# been read file by file through the Hostinger connector — 147 files, 21.21MB,
# of which 18.40MB is backups, scratch and zipped archives — and it turned up
# several things the patterns above do not catch. Each block below exists
# because of a specific file that is reachable today.
#
# NOTE: none of this is in force until the export is actually deployed. A deny
# rule in this repository protects nothing while the server still runs its own
# .htaccess. The credential below has to be rotated regardless.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Shell scripts. upload-ftp.sh sits in the web root with the FTP host, username
# and password written into it in plaintext — a write credential for the whole
# document root, readable by anyone who requests the filename. Rotating that
# password is the fix; this only stops the next one being readable.
<FilesMatch "\.(sh|bash|zsh|env|ini|conf|log|sql)$|^\.env">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# The old PHP helpers. api.php is deliberately NOT here — the admin panel calls
# it on every load — but the rest are installers and repair scripts that should
# never have been reachable. wain-inst.php is a 21KB installer.
<FilesMatch "^(wain-inst|wain-restore|wain-fix|wain-ver|wain-search-cache|v)\.php$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Build configuration that leaked out of a repository into the web root. It
# gives away dependency versions and build layout for nothing in return.
<FilesMatch "^(package|package-lock|tsconfig|composer|composer-lock)\.json$|^(next|postcss|tailwind|eslint)\.config\.(ts|js|mjs|cjs)$|^next-env\.d\.ts$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Whole copies of the old single-file app, each a few hundred KB of source with
# its own inline logic: wain-app-latest.html, qareeb.html, wain-local-test.html,
# extracted_index.html, wain-admin-latest.html.
<FilesMatch "^(wain-app-latest|wain-admin-latest|wain-local-test|qareeb|extracted_.+)\.(html|js|webmanifest)$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Dumps and checks that the -out.txt pattern misses because they are named
# differently: *-check.txt, verify.txt, cache-selftest.txt, sentinel-live-urls
# .json, rashed-v2.json.
#
# index.txt is deliberately NOT here, though the server carries a 92KB one from
# the old app. This export writes an index.txt of its own beside every single
# index.html — 45 of them, the App Router's prefetch payloads — so a rule on
# that name would break client-side navigation on every route of the new site
# to tidy away one stale file that the deploy overwrites anyway. Checked
# against out/ rather than guessed; the first draft of this block had it and
# would have shipped the bug.
<FilesMatch "-check\.txt$|^(verify|cache-selftest|claude-upload-test)\.txt$|^(sentinel-live-urls|rashed-v2)\.json$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Internal notes. Markdown in a web root is documentation for an attacker as
# readily as for a maintainer; wain-db-audit.md describes the database.
<FilesMatch "\.md$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Caching
#
# Two classes of file, and they need opposite policies:
#
#   1. /_next/static/**  — every .js, .css and .woff2 carries a content hash in
#      its filename, so a changed file is a *different URL*. These can be
#      cached for a year and never revalidated. `immutable` also stops browsers
#      re-checking them on reload.
#
#   2. Everything else — index.html, og.png, sitemap.xml … keep stable names,
#      so they must revalidate or a deploy would be invisible to returning
#      visitors. `no-cache` still allows 304s via ETag: cheap when unchanged,
#      correct when changed.
#
# A build guard (scripts/check-cache-safety.mjs) fails the build if an
# unhashed .js/.css/.woff2 ever appears outside /_next/static/, which would
# make the immutable rule below unsafe.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  # 1. Content-hashed build output — cache hard, forever.
  <FilesMatch "\.(js|mjs|css|woff2|woff)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
  </FilesMatch>

  # 1b. The service worker is the one unhashed .js we ship, and it decides
  # which build every installed app runs. It must never be frozen by rule 1,
  # so this comes after it and wins.
  <Files "sw.js">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate"
    Header set Service-Worker-Allowed "/"
  </Files>

  # 2a. HTML and the RSC payloads beside it — always revalidate.
  <FilesMatch "\.(html|txt)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>

  # 2b. Stable-named media (incl. صوت وين clips) — a week in cache, then
  # revalidate.
  <FilesMatch "\.(png|jpg|jpeg|webp|avif|svg|ico|mp3)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400"
  </FilesMatch>

  # 2c. Crawler and install metadata — short, so changes propagate quickly.
  <FilesMatch "\.(xml|webmanifest|json)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=3600"
  </FilesMatch>

  # Never let a proxy serve the wrong encoding.
  Header append Vary Accept-Encoding
</IfModule>

# Fallback for hosts without mod_headers.
<IfModule mod_expires.c>
  ExpiresActive On
  ExpiresDefault                      "access plus 1 hour"
  ExpiresByType text/html             "access plus 0 seconds"
  ExpiresByType text/css              "access plus 1 year"
  ExpiresByType application/javascript "access plus 1 year"
  ExpiresByType font/woff2            "access plus 1 year"
  ExpiresByType font/woff             "access plus 1 year"
  ExpiresByType image/png             "access plus 1 week"
  ExpiresByType image/svg+xml         "access plus 1 week"
  ExpiresByType image/x-icon          "access plus 1 week"
  ExpiresByType audio/mpeg            "access plus 1 week"
</IfModule>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compression
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Brotli first where available — noticeably smaller than gzip for text.
<IfModule mod_brotli.c>
  AddOutputFilterByType BROTLI_COMPRESS text/html text/css text/plain text/xml \
    application/javascript application/json application/manifest+json image/svg+xml
</IfModule>

<IfModule mod_deflate.c>
  AddOutputFilterByType DEFLATE text/html text/css text/plain text/xml \
    application/javascript application/json application/manifest+json image/svg+xml
</IfModule>

# woff2 is already compressed; re-compressing wastes CPU and can grow it.
<IfModule mod_setenvif.c>
  SetEnvIfNoCase Request_URI \.(woff2?|png|jpe?g|webp|avif|ico)$ no-gzip dont-vary
</IfModule>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Correct types (some hosts do not know these by default)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
<IfModule mod_mime.c>
  AddType font/woff2 .woff2
  AddType application/manifest+json .webmanifest
  AddType image/svg+xml .svg
</IfModule>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Baseline security headers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header set X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
  Header set Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
  # شوق needs the microphone; nothing else on the site needs these features.
  Header set Permissions-Policy "camera=(), geolocation=(self), microphone=(self)"

  # Nobody has any business framing this site. /admin is a real session behind
  # this, so being framable is a clickjacking route into it. frame-ancestors is
  # the modern control; X-Frame-Options covers browsers that predate it.
  Header set X-Frame-Options "DENY"

  # The site is HTTPS-only on Hostinger. Deliberately without includeSubDomains
  # and without preload: both are hard to walk back, and a subdomain that is
  # not yet on HTTPS would become unreachable for a year. Add them once every
  # subdomain is confirmed HTTPS.
  Header always set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"

  # No cookies leave this domain. Ever.
  #
  # Nothing in the site sets one — the build is static files, there is no PHP
  # in the request path, and audit:cookies loads ten pages in a real browser
  # and asserts the jar comes back empty. So why strip a header nothing sends?
  #
  # Because the thing that would send it is not ours. Shared hosting adds
  # cookies on its own account: LiteSpeed's cache does it to vary responses,
  # bot-protection and "under attack" layers do it to mark a browser as
  # cleared, and both arrive by a control-panel toggle rather than a commit —
  # nobody edits this repository, the site quietly gains a cookie, and the
  # promise on /privacy silently becomes false. This makes that impossible
  # instead of unlikely: whatever the host decides to attach, the visitor
  # never receives it.
  #
  # Safe precisely because the site has no session to lose. Orders and queue
  # tickets are held in the visitor's own localStorage and authenticated to
  # Supabase by a token in the request body, never by a cookie — so there is
  # no logged-in state for this to break. Anything added later that DOES need
  # a cookie has to delete this line, which is the point: it cannot happen by
  # accident, and whoever deletes it has to answer for /privacy too.
  Header always unset Set-Cookie
  Header always unset Set-Cookie2

  # Content Security Policy.
  #
  # Honest about its limits: 'unsafe-inline' has to stay in script-src because
  # Next.js inlines its hydration payload and a static export has no server to
  # mint a per-request nonce. So this is not a strong defence against injected
  # inline script. What it does buy, and what the site actually needs:
  #
  #   * script-src pins executable code to this origin and unpkg (شوق's widget)
  #     — nothing else can be loaded, whatever ends up in the DOM.
  #   * frame-ancestors 'none' blocks clickjacking of /admin.
  #   * form-action 'self' stops an injected form posting credentials offsite.
  #   * base-uri 'self' stops a <base> tag re-pointing every relative URL.
  #   * object-src 'none' removes the plugin surface entirely.
  #   * connect-src names Supabase, ElevenLabs and the n8n speech bridge
  #     explicitly, so exfiltration to an arbitrary host is blocked rather than
  #     merely unlikely.
  #
  # The bridge host is here because connect-src is where a feature goes to die
  # quietly. NEXT_PUBLIC_WAIN_TTS_URL turns on شوق's live voice for sentences
  # with no recorded clip, and with the host missing every one of those calls is
  # refused by the browser — the site falls back to the robot voice, the deploy
  # log still reports «live bridge», and nothing anywhere says why. Setting the
  # variable without this line is a switch wired to nothing.
  #
  # frame-src is openstreetmap.org for the maps. If شوق or the voice stop
  # working after a change here, the browser console names the directive.
  Header always set Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://*.supabase.co; font-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://unpkg.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://unpkg.com https://api.elevenlabs.io https://api.us.elevenlabs.io wss://api.elevenlabs.io wss://api.us.elevenlabs.io https://sportake.app.n8n.cloud; frame-src https://www.openstreetmap.org; media-src 'self' blob: https://api.elevenlabs.io; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'"
</IfModule>
